rride files are read verbatim (no trimming, no\nrendering, no defanging); a read failure is a plain `Error` with the 2.14\nprefixes. Callers pass paths already resolved through the config's\n`promptPath` (ticket 05); this module does not resolve them.\n\n`renderFinderUser` and `renderVerifierUser` are typed TS functions that\nreproduce the baseline `finder_user.tmpl` / `verifier_user.tmpl` output\nexactly (2.16, 2.17), with `dataText` defanging closing wrapper tags using\nRE2 semantics (ASCII `\\s`, Unicode simple case folding, ASCII word\nboundary) and `formatFixed2` from `gocompat` for confidence. U+2014\ncharacters in copied template lines are written as `\\u2014` escapes in\nthe TS source.\n\nTemporary differential test (deleted at M6 with the harness): under\n`test/diff/`, run by `npm run test:diff`, render both user prompts in Go\nand in TS from the same inputs and compare bytes. Reuse ticket 09's\nbaseline mechanism (worktree at `cd08f10`, `GOFLAGS` removed, cache under\n`node_modules/.cache/roast-diff/`) to build a small Go helper that calls\nthe baseline `prompts.FinderUser` / `prompts.VerifierUser` on JSON input;\nskip with a TAP skip when `go` is not on `PATH`, as the harness does.\nInputs must include a hostile case (closing tags in mixed case, `ſ`,\n`\\v`, `</claimx`), a survey case, and the 0.125-multiple confidence ties.\n\nThe finder stage (`find`, tool schemas, validation) is ticket 16.\n\n## Acceptance criteria\n\n- [ ] Each of the twelve imported template strings equals the bytes of\n  its file under `internal/prompts/templates/` decoded as UTF-8.\n- [ ] `classifyMode` returns `code` for an empty list, `prose` when every\n  extension is prose, `mixed` when some are, `code` when none, and\n  compares extensions case-insensitively; `docs/.md` counts as prose.\n- [ ] `classifyLangs` maps, dedupes, and sorts tags and ignores unknown\n  extensions.\n- [ ] `resolveLangs` returns `[]` for prose without validating flags,\n  auto-classifies with no flag values, returns `[]` for a lone `none`,\n  throws `UsageError` for `none` combined with another pack and for an\n  unknown pack (case-sensitive, untrimmed), and otherwise keeps flag\n  order and duplicates.\n- [ ] `finderSystem` output contains the expected template assets in the\n  expected order for prose, code, and mixed modes in both `diff` and\n  `repo` scope (asserted by asset containment and index order, not\n  wording); prose diff mode has no diff framing.\n- [ ] The frontend addendum appears once for `react`, `frontend`, or\n  both; the hooks addendum only for `react`; the go addendum only for\n  `go`; `web` adds nothing; the quick addendum is always last.\n- [ ] An override replaces only the base, byte for byte, while scope,\n  mixed, language, and quick pieces still appear; a missing override\n  file rejects with an `Error` that is not a `UsageError`.\n- [ ] `verifierSystem` returns the override verbatim when given and the\n  `verifier_system` asset otherwise.\n- [ ] `renderFinderUser` survey output contains a `<manifest>` block and\n  no `<diff>` or `<files>` block; diff output contains `<diff>` and\n  `<files>` and no `<manifest>`.\n- [ ] `renderVerifierUser` output never contains the finder's reasoning\n  (the type has no such field) and, for untrusted text containing\n  closing tags, each wrapper tag closes exactly once and the final\n  instruction line is last.\n- [ ] `dataText` defangs `</CODE_QUOTE >` and a `ſ`-folded `</claim`,\n  and leaves `</\\vclaim` and `</claimx` unchanged.\n- [ ] The temporary differential test produces byte-identical\n  `finder_user` and `verifier_user` renderings from Go and TS for every\n  fixture input, and reports a skip (exit 0) when `go` is unavailable.\n- [ ] `npm run lint`, `npm run typecheck`, and the TS test suite pass,\n  and the Go build and Go tests still pass.\n\n\nThese are records of earlier runs. The ticket or spec may have changed since then; where they disagree, follow the ticket and spec. Do not repeat an