ODE_QUOTE` doesn't perfectly align with `code_quote` in the alternation, so the match fails partway through.\n\nI also need to account for the space before the `>`. The space gets consumed by the `[ \\t\\n\\r ]*` portion, which is why the test output shows the space being removed from the final result. The space after `CODE_QUOTE` gets consumed by the optional whitespace pattern, so the regex matches `</CODE_QUOTE` without the trailing space. The match position lands at 13, right at the `>`, which isn't an ASCII word character, so it gets replaced with `</`. The test output shows `</CODE_QUOTE >` with the space intact, confirming the regex captured the tag and whitespace correctly.\n\nI'm realizing the test failures might stem from the `u` flag and Unicode handling in the regex pattern, or possibly from how the template files are being processed. Let me add some debugging to trace what's actually happening during execution.\n"}}
